From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:02:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: floppy disks on the storage, save disks by
 content hash; backup API

Zipped floppies are unpacked to /storage/floppy_disks instead of a 16 MB
RAM disk (RAM only without the storage): the ST's saves survive a
power-off. A disk's folder is "<name>-<hash of its contents>", looked up
by the hash, so the same disk finds its saves whatever its name, path or
source. Plain .st/.msa images from the library's download folders are
copied into such a folder on insert and written there (the download stays
as it came); other image files are written in place as before. Folders
the ST wrote to are marked and kept; the rest is a cache (128 MB).

/api/v1/system/backup: what a backup holds, the backup itself (made by
the image's ce-backup as it's sent, chunked), and restore (upload).
