+// Zipped floppy images are unpacked on insert into FLOPPY_DISKS_DIR on the
+// CosmosEx's own storage (the SD card: faster than a floppy, and the ST's
+// saves survive a power-off), or into UNPACK_RAM_DIR when the storage isn't
+// mounted. One folder per disk, named "<file name>-<hash>": the hash of the
+// original file's contents (SHA-256, 16 hex digits), so the same disk finds
+// its folder whatever its path, name or source (downloaded again, from
+// another list, moved, restored from a backup). Kept after eject: inserting
+// the same disk again uses it, with what the ST wrote to it.
+//
+// The same for plain .st/.msa images from the floppy library (a download
+// folder: isLibraryImage): copied into such a folder on insert, so the ST's
+// saves go to the copy and are found again for that disk; the download
+// stays as it came. Image files elsewhere (your own, on USB, the shared
+// drive, translated folders) are written in place, as before.
+//
+// A folder the ST has written to gets UNPACK_WRITTEN_MARKER and is kept for
+// good (a save disk: it goes into the backup, ce-backup). The others are
+// a cache: above UNPACK_STORAGE_BUDGET (or when the RAM disk is full) the
+// least recently inserted go first; a folder an inserted image comes from
+// is never deleted. Image files on the storage itself are saved in place;
+// those the ST wrote to are listed in FLOPPY_WRITTEN_LIST (for the backup).
